1
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:06,920
How could you do this?

2
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:08,760
-Come home with me. -Let go.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Leave me alone.

4
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:15,840
This is Mrs. Arisara.

5
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:18,360
She's in charge of investment and management.

6
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:20,360
I guess P'Ing and Itt never told you

7
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:22,040
who the real victim was.

8
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:23,880
Just because I used to like you,

9
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:25,640
does that mean I owe you something?

10
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:27,400
What happened between you two?

11
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:29,160
I'm sorry, P'Ing.

12
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:30,960
Yok and I aren't together anymore.

13
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:32,920
-Yok... -I love P'Ing

14
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,280
so much that I can't even control myself.

15
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:57,040
You can't just run away from your responsibilities.

16
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:01,120
Yok won't listen to anyone.

17
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,360
He's even given up on his studies.

18
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:05,920
And my father

19
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,480
will never agree to compromise.

20
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:11,760
I'm begging you to help me.

21
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:14,000
Please.

22
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:16,360
Look, Mr. Phet.

23
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:18,280
This is not my responsibility.

24
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:20,760
Yok and I aren't together anymore.

25
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:23,480
Whatever happens to him

26
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:25,039
has nothing to do with me.

27
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:26,680
Is that all you had to say?

28
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:28,080
I'm hanging up.

29
00:03:54,720 --> 00:03:56,560
It's so damn hot. What's with this crazy weather?

30
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:58,160
Should we walk that way for a bit?

31
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:13,680
Mr. Ing.

32
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:19,880
How did you get here?

33
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:21,000
What?

34
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:22,240
Aren't you happy to see me?

35
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:24,800
Of course I am.

36
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:28,080
And I've missed you so much.

37
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:30,720
Come on.

38
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:32,120
Let's go.

39
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:44,560
Come on, one last shot.

40
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:47,480
Mr. Ing, take it slow.

41
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:51,000
It's fine. It's a welcome-home drink.

42
00:04:58,200 --> 00:04:59,560
I'll lie down over there.

43
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:01,080
Okay.

44
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:15,280
Do you want a head massage?

45
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:17,480
I've taken massage classes before.

46
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:20,760
My instructor even said I have a great touch.

47
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:21,960
Sure.

48
00:05:33,159 --> 00:05:34,320
Can I sit right here?

49
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:47,000
That's perfect.

50
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:54,000
Hey, Junior.

51
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:55,720
Yes?

52
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:58,920
I'm just a nobody with no job now.

53
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:01,280
On top of that, I'm crashing here at your place

54
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,840
and not even paying rent.

55
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:08,000
And you still have to wait on me hand and foot.

56
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:10,840
Please don't think like that.

57
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,040
I know what you've been going through.

58
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:16,440
How did you know about that?

59
00:06:16,640 --> 00:06:18,640
The internet is full of news about you.

60
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:22,040
I've read a bit of it.

61
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:26,600
Do you feel better now, Mr. Ing?

62
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:27,800
That's enough.

63
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:30,560
Stop calling me "Mr. Ing" all the time.

64
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:32,120
It feels so distant, you know?

65
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:33,600
Can you call me something else?

66
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,560
Then, what should I call you?

67
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:39,720
How about...

68
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:41,720
-"P'Ing"? -Don't call me that.

69
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:48,159
Call me anything except P'Ing.

70
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:52,320
Then, what should I call you?

71
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:54,720
Just Ing is fine.

72
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:57,640
Are you sure about that?

73
00:06:57,840 --> 00:06:58,840
Of course.

74
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:01,200
What's wrong with it?

75
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:04,840
Ing...

76
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:06,800
Ing...

77
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,320
Okay.

78
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:14,560
Just call me the way you did if it's that hard.

79
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:17,200
In that case, I'll call you what I did.

80
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,160
Junior.

81
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:20,280
Yes?

82
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:25,280
School starts next week, right?

83
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:26,720
You have to go to class, don't you?

84
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:28,280
That's right.

85
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:32,120
Okay.

86
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:33,680
I'll go pick you up.

87
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:43,920
You're being really nice to me.

88
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:50,320
It's actually you

89
00:07:52,440 --> 00:07:53,680
who's been nice to me.

90
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:04,280
Yeah, that's exactly the spot.

91
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:31,600
See ya.

92
00:08:34,520 --> 00:08:35,919
P'Juju.

93
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:41,000
Why are you here?

94
00:08:44,039 --> 00:08:45,600
I told you to call me Junior.

95
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:47,720
You weren't answering my messages,

96
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:49,200
so I came to see you.

97
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:54,720
Your friend is so handsome.

98
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:56,840
Are you an actor or an idol?

99
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:57,880
No, I'm neither.

100
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:07,600
I told you to call me Junior.

101
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:12,760
Fine.

102
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:17,040
Let me...

103
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:19,440
talk to my friend for a second.

104
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:20,720
Okay.

105
00:09:32,720 --> 00:09:33,840
"Juju," huh?

106
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:38,160
That's what my family calls me.

107
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:40,760
She just picked it up from them.

108
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:45,400
Be honest with me.

109
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:48,400
Is she your girlfriend?

110
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:52,640
We grew up together.

111
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:55,000
My mom told me a few days ago

112
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:56,920
that she'd be coming here for school,

113
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:59,120
and she asked me to look after her.

114
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:04,520
But I didn't expect she'd come here... today.

115
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:15,600
You know how to drive, right?

116
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:18,840
Take her to get some good food

117
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:20,960
and buy any essentials for her stay here.

118
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:23,600
-Ing... -She came all this way to see you.

119
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:25,040
Just show her around.

120
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:27,040
Don't be so hard on her, okay?

121
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:29,040
Be nice to her.

122
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:36,520
I'll have your "P'Juju"

123
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:38,200
take you out for a delicious meal.

124
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:38,960
Okay.

125
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:43,000
Have fun.

126
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,320
Thank you.

127
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:50,080
Wait, why is he leaving already?

128
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:11,600
Mr. Yok,

129
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:13,600
you need to eat something.

130
00:13:13,640 --> 00:13:16,200
You haven't touched your food in two days.

131
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:20,000
Come in.

132
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:43,400
What the hell is wrong with you?

133
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:46,640
P'Ing...

134
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:48,880
Please come home with me.

135
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:51,800
Come home? What are you talking about?

136
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:53,480
Plenty of people

137
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:54,880
want me to go home with them.

138
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:55,880
Why do I have to go with you?

139
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:57,520
You're so full of yourself.

140
00:14:57,920 --> 00:14:59,600
You freaking reek of booze.

141
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:02,200
Please come home with me.

142
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:03,320
Jeez.

143
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:04,680
What the hell is this?

144
00:15:07,080 --> 00:15:09,440
-Come home with me. -Listen to me.

145
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:10,240
Look.

146
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:11,880
-Damn, how come you have so much strength? -Let's go home.

147
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:13,280
I... Dammit.

148
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:14,080
Let go of me.

149
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:17,000
Listen to me.

150
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:19,560
My mom is dead.

151
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:20,760
My dad remarried.

152
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:22,360
I don't have a home or anything left.

153
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:24,800
What did I do wrong? Today's just not my day.

154
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:26,400
I'll find a home for you.

155
00:15:26,520 --> 00:15:27,280
P'Ing...

156
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:29,720
Let go of me.

157
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:32,440
I might not be able to help you much yet,

158
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:36,160
but I will be the one you can count on.

159
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:37,280
-Listen to me. -P'Ing.

160
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:39,200
I'm so freaking exhausted.

161
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:41,360
Seriously, let me ask you.

162
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:42,400
Hey, Yok.

163
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:43,000
I...

164
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:45,800
Damn, what are you trying to do now?

165
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:47,880
Just listen to me.

166
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:50,560
God, I'm so tired.

167
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:51,200
Seriously,

168
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:52,520
do all ministers teach their kids

169
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:54,240
to be this shameless?

170
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:55,960
You just won't stop pestering me.

171
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:57,800
P'Ing...

172
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:04,760
Yok, listen to me.

173
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:06,080
Back when I was crazy about you,

174
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:06,760
remember what you said?

175
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:07,920
You found me disgusting.

176
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:09,400
And what are we now?

177
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:11,240
You had the nerve to tell your family you love me.

178
00:16:11,280 --> 00:16:13,080
Have you completely lost your freaking mind?

179
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:17,280
Did P'Phet tell you that?

180
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:20,800
Yeah, he did.

181
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:22,720
And I don't want to know

182
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:23,800
a thing about you.

183
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:25,400
You'd better make things clear with your brother

184
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:26,280
and figure out what to do.

185
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:27,920
Just stay the hell out of my life.

186
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:30,280
P'Ing...

187
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:34,400
I always thought

188
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:37,200
that I'd just live a normal life,

189
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:40,800
but after meeting you,

190
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:43,080
I can't do that anymore.

191
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:48,200
I'm going to keep loving you...

192
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:51,920
even if you never forgive me.

193
00:16:55,280 --> 00:16:57,280
I won't look for anyone else for the rest of my life.

194
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:03,720
Please give me a chance,

195
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:05,440
P'Ing.

196
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:12,800
Listen to me very carefully.

197
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:17,160
A privileged brat like you

198
00:17:17,319 --> 00:17:19,200
can't expect everything to go your way.

199
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:23,560
Just look at yourself.

200
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:25,440
You're so freaking pathetic.

201
00:17:27,160 --> 00:17:28,920
Nothing lasts forever

202
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:30,280
the way you want it to.

203
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:32,320
Now let me go.

204
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:35,360
Dammit.

205
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:40,280
P'Ing.

206
00:17:40,760 --> 00:17:41,680
P'Ing...

207
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:44,000
P'Ing.

208
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:45,960
-P'Ing. -Stop knocking already.

209
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,040
-Please give me a chance. -Go away.

210
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:47,800
P'Ing...

211
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:49,800
P'Ing.

212
00:17:50,080 --> 00:17:51,400
Let's go home together.

213
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:53,280
P'Ing.

214
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:54,760
Go to hell, you idiot.

215
00:17:56,920 --> 00:17:57,800
P'Ing...

216
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:01,080
Dammit.

217
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:24,920
Why is it so loud?

218
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:30,520
How did he end up here?

219
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:34,000
He was sleeping outside last night.

220
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:35,240
It was cold,

221
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:37,360
so I was worried he'd get sick.

222
00:21:37,360 --> 00:21:39,200
Why didn't you just chase him away?

223
00:21:39,280 --> 00:21:40,800
How was I supposed to do that?

224
00:21:41,840 --> 00:21:43,920
Who the hell is calling this early?

225
00:21:50,440 --> 00:21:51,240
Hello?

226
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:53,680
Yok, where are you?

227
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:54,720
Hold on, Mr. Phet.

228
00:21:54,800 --> 00:21:55,720
This is Ing,

229
00:21:55,920 --> 00:21:57,080
Tiwakorn.

230
00:21:58,280 --> 00:21:59,920
Is my brother with you, Mr. Ing?

231
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:01,360
You...

232
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:02,400
Stop right there.

233
00:22:02,480 --> 00:22:04,680
He just came running up to me, wagging his tail and all.

234
00:22:04,680 --> 00:22:06,040
It's a real mess right now.

235
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:07,480
I'll send you the location.

236
00:22:07,520 --> 00:22:09,200
Please hurry up.

237
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:15,440
Why did you let him in?

238
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:32,280
Ing,

239
00:22:32,840 --> 00:22:33,960
please have some soup.

240
00:22:34,360 --> 00:22:35,160
Okay.

241
00:22:43,320 --> 00:22:44,800
What did you just call him?

242
00:22:46,800 --> 00:22:48,320
How is that any of your business?

243
00:22:48,360 --> 00:22:50,040
It's his place. Why are you insulting him?

244
00:22:50,080 --> 00:22:50,600
You actually let him

245
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:51,760
-call you that? -Yeah.

246
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:52,720
So what?

247
00:22:53,560 --> 00:22:55,320
How long have you been staying here?

248
00:22:56,960 --> 00:22:58,280
Isn't that my business?

249
00:22:58,440 --> 00:23:00,200
Are you that into him?

250
00:23:02,120 --> 00:23:02,880
Yeah.

251
00:23:03,800 --> 00:23:05,040
He's nice to me.

252
00:23:05,120 --> 00:23:06,360
He never lies to me,

253
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:07,840
and he doesn't backstab me.

254
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:10,640
He gets me whatever I want. Why?

255
00:23:17,040 --> 00:23:18,120
Who the hell are you

256
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:19,400
to even compare yourself to him?

257
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:26,960
So, you and him...

258
00:23:27,200 --> 00:23:28,480
have slept together?

259
00:23:30,520 --> 00:23:31,560
You've got to be kidding me.

260
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:33,000
Mr. Yok,

261
00:23:33,520 --> 00:23:34,440
you should leave.

262
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:35,480
Stay out of this.

263
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:37,160
This is between him and me.

264
00:23:49,760 --> 00:23:50,800
Just get out of here.

265
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:53,200
-Leave. -Why?

266
00:23:53,520 --> 00:23:54,680
If I leave, then what?

267
00:23:54,720 --> 00:23:56,560
You'll live happily ever after with him?

268
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:58,400
What does he have that I don't?

269
00:23:58,960 --> 00:24:00,160
You've clearly lost your mind.

270
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:01,440
This is not your place.

271
00:24:01,480 --> 00:24:02,440
Get out.

272
00:24:05,560 --> 00:24:07,400
You forced your way into my life

273
00:24:07,440 --> 00:24:09,080
even though I didn't want you to.

274
00:24:09,320 --> 00:24:11,320
Don't think you can just dump me.

275
00:24:12,880 --> 00:24:14,800
I won't let you date anyone else.

276
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:15,800
Yok,

277
00:24:16,360 --> 00:24:17,600
are you insane?

278
00:24:17,680 --> 00:24:19,160
This is not your place.

279
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:21,800
-Get out. -I'm not leaving.

280
00:24:23,320 --> 00:24:25,320
You'll be with me for the rest of your life,

281
00:24:25,840 --> 00:24:29,320
even if I have to spend mine making it up to you.

282
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:48,600
Junior,

283
00:24:49,520 --> 00:24:50,520
get the door.

284
00:24:53,280 --> 00:24:54,520
And go in your room.

285
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:18,880
Don't you think you've embarrassed yourself enough?

286
00:25:20,840 --> 00:25:21,680
P'Phet,

287
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:23,280
please stay out of my business.

288
00:25:23,560 --> 00:25:25,000
You can't force me.

289
00:25:26,520 --> 00:25:27,400
Yok...

290
00:25:41,080 --> 00:25:41,880
Mr. Ing,

291
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:45,000
you said it was over between you and him

292
00:25:45,800 --> 00:25:48,080
and that you didn't care about what happened to him.

293
00:25:49,200 --> 00:25:51,200
Just to be clear with my brother,

294
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:54,000
did you actually mean it?

295
00:26:07,200 --> 00:26:08,000
I did.

296
00:26:14,360 --> 00:26:15,480
Are you happy now?

297
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:17,720
As for your brother,

298
00:26:17,760 --> 00:26:20,080
I called the police on him. Happy now?

299
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:29,440
Happy now?

300
00:26:35,800 --> 00:26:36,720
Good.

301
00:26:37,400 --> 00:26:39,720
Then you two don't need to see each other anymore.

302
00:26:40,080 --> 00:26:41,480
It'll be better for our peace of mind

303
00:26:42,680 --> 00:26:44,400
and for yours, too.

304
00:26:50,920 --> 00:26:52,000
Exactly.

305
00:26:52,320 --> 00:26:54,160
We'll be better off this way.

306
00:26:59,760 --> 00:27:00,440
Yok,

307
00:27:01,640 --> 00:27:02,400
come with me.

308
00:27:41,240 --> 00:27:42,800
I'm moving out in two days.

309
00:27:46,960 --> 00:27:49,120
Work has been pretty heavy,

310
00:27:49,320 --> 00:27:50,720
and this place is far from the office.

311
00:27:52,560 --> 00:27:53,440
Besides,

312
00:27:56,680 --> 00:27:58,480
I'm afraid someone might come bother you.

313
00:28:02,960 --> 00:28:03,880
Ing,

314
00:28:05,400 --> 00:28:06,080
are you...

315
00:28:07,880 --> 00:28:09,160
actually...

316
00:28:11,200 --> 00:28:12,320
leaving?

317
00:28:16,320 --> 00:28:17,600
That girl...

318
00:28:20,920 --> 00:28:22,400
She really likes you, doesn't she?

319
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:25,120
She...

320
00:28:25,960 --> 00:28:27,880
Well, actually...

321
00:28:28,080 --> 00:28:30,080
my mom wants her to be my girlfriend.

322
00:28:31,440 --> 00:28:34,040
My mom set us up,

323
00:28:34,160 --> 00:28:36,080
but I don't have feelings for her.

324
00:28:37,200 --> 00:28:38,400
She moved to Bangkok,

325
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:39,800
and she needs someone to look after her,

326
00:28:39,800 --> 00:28:41,160
so I have to be that person.

327
00:28:41,280 --> 00:28:43,840
I just thought... I was helping her out.

328
00:28:45,800 --> 00:28:47,680
Maybe she can be my girlfriend.

329
00:28:48,080 --> 00:28:49,000
Wait, no.

330
00:28:49,240 --> 00:28:50,160
I meant to say "my friend."

331
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:52,800
I...

332
00:28:54,120 --> 00:28:54,840
I just...

333
00:28:55,880 --> 00:28:57,560
-I don't really know, either. -Junior.

334
00:28:58,720 --> 00:29:00,560
I don't know what your family situation is

335
00:29:00,600 --> 00:29:03,040
or why they want you to get married or have kids.

336
00:29:04,920 --> 00:29:06,080
But seriously,

337
00:29:07,040 --> 00:29:08,800
I want you to think this through carefully

338
00:29:10,040 --> 00:29:11,080
instead of wasting your time on me.

339
00:29:11,120 --> 00:29:12,280
I'm not wasting my time.

340
00:29:12,560 --> 00:29:14,000
I don't like her.

341
00:29:14,200 --> 00:29:15,840
It's impossible anyway

342
00:29:17,120 --> 00:29:18,720
for us to stay together forever, isn't it?

343
00:29:26,560 --> 00:29:27,320
Look.

344
00:29:31,040 --> 00:29:32,360
When you get married,

345
00:29:34,400 --> 00:29:36,200
I'll make sure to give you a generous gift.

346
00:29:43,880 --> 00:29:45,520
Thank you so much for everything.

347
00:30:54,600 --> 00:30:55,680
Hi, Mom.

348
00:31:00,400 --> 00:31:01,320
Do you like it?

349
00:31:04,240 --> 00:31:05,520
I bet you're surprised

350
00:31:05,560 --> 00:31:07,920
that I knew which wine was your favorite.

351
00:31:27,360 --> 00:31:28,440
[Born: April 26, 1979]

352
00:31:28,440 --> 00:31:29,440
[Died: September 6, 2026]

353
00:31:29,480 --> 00:31:30,600
You first, Mom.

354
00:31:50,360 --> 00:31:51,080
Mom...

355
00:31:57,000 --> 00:31:59,480
You know, this favorite wine of yours

356
00:32:00,560 --> 00:32:02,000
tastes incredible.

357
00:32:04,440 --> 00:32:06,600
I guess I got my good taste

358
00:32:08,280 --> 00:32:09,520
from you, huh?

359
00:32:15,440 --> 00:32:16,600
It's nothing, really.

360
00:32:21,920 --> 00:32:24,080
I'm just trying to talk to you.

361
00:32:29,680 --> 00:32:30,640
You know what?

362
00:32:33,520 --> 00:32:34,680
The thing is...

363
00:32:35,440 --> 00:32:38,680
my life's been pretty damn exciting, Mom.

364
00:32:42,840 --> 00:32:45,080
I was seeing someone.

365
00:32:48,200 --> 00:32:49,520
Do you know how it turned out?

366
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:54,680
We didn't make it.

367
00:32:57,160 --> 00:32:58,960
It all went up in flames.

368
00:33:01,760 --> 00:33:04,200
The company I worked so hard to build

369
00:33:04,200 --> 00:33:06,040
was stolen by my brother.

370
00:33:08,440 --> 00:33:10,480
At least I managed to get the house back...

371
00:33:12,400 --> 00:33:15,200
even though it doesn't look or feel like...

372
00:33:15,480 --> 00:33:18,200
the home we once shared.

373
00:33:30,400 --> 00:33:32,080
I don't even know what's wrong with me.

374
00:33:35,120 --> 00:33:37,160
Even the smallest problem makes me feel like

375
00:33:37,160 --> 00:33:38,800
I'm about to fall apart.

376
00:33:43,080 --> 00:33:45,960
If last year's version of me saw me like this,

377
00:33:45,960 --> 00:33:48,120
he'd knock me flat on my face.

378
00:33:50,920 --> 00:33:53,080
I'm nothing but a pathetic loser.

379
00:33:58,400 --> 00:33:59,600
If you were still here...

380
00:34:04,760 --> 00:34:06,800
would you see me as one, too?

381
00:34:09,800 --> 00:34:11,800
[Ravipa Adularaya]

382
00:34:11,840 --> 00:34:13,600
At this point, it feels like...

383
00:34:18,440 --> 00:34:20,600
I don't know how to trust anyone anymore.

384
00:34:25,560 --> 00:34:28,880
The person I gave everything to...

385
00:34:33,080 --> 00:34:35,199
turned out to be the one who hurt me the most.

386
00:34:38,080 --> 00:34:40,239
I guess I really am your son.

387
00:34:50,400 --> 00:34:52,360
If anyone ever says I'm a bad person,

388
00:34:52,400 --> 00:34:54,560
it's your fault for not being here to set me straight.

389
00:34:54,560 --> 00:34:56,199
Why did you have to leave so soon?

390
00:35:01,400 --> 00:35:04,120
Why did you leave me to face everything on my own?

391
00:35:11,080 --> 00:35:12,040
You know what?

392
00:35:17,840 --> 00:35:19,120
I hate you.

393
00:35:22,160 --> 00:35:23,800
I hate you, Mom.

394
00:35:26,160 --> 00:35:27,760
I really do.

395
00:35:44,680 --> 00:35:46,720
But I also miss you so much.

396
00:35:55,760 --> 00:35:57,400
What the hell is wrong with me?

397
00:36:01,040 --> 00:36:03,280
Why am I here crying in front of you?

398
00:36:18,520 --> 00:36:20,520
I'm going to stay and keep you company.

399
00:36:22,920 --> 00:36:24,520
I just can't take it anymore.

400
00:36:44,160 --> 00:36:48,320
[Ravipa Adularaya]

401
00:36:48,320 --> 00:36:49,960
[Born: April 26, 1979]

402
00:36:50,000 --> 00:36:51,680
[Died: September 6, 2026]

403
00:36:57,800 --> 00:36:59,120
Drink some water and sober up

404
00:36:59,640 --> 00:37:01,080
before going inside.

405
00:37:05,160 --> 00:37:06,600
If he'd actually cared about you,

406
00:37:07,080 --> 00:37:08,880
would he have let me take you away?

407
00:37:09,200 --> 00:37:12,200
Can't you see it? He's already moved on.

408
00:37:13,600 --> 00:37:15,200
It's over between you two.

409
00:37:15,200 --> 00:37:16,200
It's not over yet.

410
00:37:16,600 --> 00:37:17,960
I can feel that he still cares about me.

411
00:37:17,960 --> 00:37:18,520
Yok,

412
00:37:19,480 --> 00:37:21,800
can you stop acting so pathetic?

413
00:37:22,080 --> 00:37:23,000
Do you have any idea

414
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:24,160
how badly it breaks my heart

415
00:37:24,160 --> 00:37:25,600
to see you like this?

416
00:37:26,600 --> 00:37:27,480
P'Phet,

417
00:37:27,800 --> 00:37:29,400
in my entire life,

418
00:37:29,440 --> 00:37:31,440
I've never loved anyone this much.

419
00:37:32,560 --> 00:37:33,960
I know it's hard to understand.

420
00:37:34,080 --> 00:37:35,760
You can think I'm crazy if you want.

421
00:37:36,440 --> 00:37:38,560
What made you turn into a different person?

422
00:37:43,680 --> 00:37:44,800
I'm not a different person.

423
00:37:46,720 --> 00:37:48,560
This Yok you're seeing right now

424
00:37:49,080 --> 00:37:50,320
is the real me.

425
00:38:07,920 --> 00:38:09,800
If it doesn't end well, don't bother coming back.

426
00:38:40,320 --> 00:38:41,160
Young man,

427
00:38:41,840 --> 00:38:43,800
you can't sleep here. It's cold.

428
00:38:44,080 --> 00:38:45,400
Are you alright?

429
00:38:45,440 --> 00:38:46,400
You okay?

430
00:38:49,800 --> 00:38:52,400
Oh, it's nothing. I just...

431
00:38:53,360 --> 00:38:55,400
nodded off.

432
00:39:00,480 --> 00:39:01,760
What time is it?

433
00:39:03,200 --> 00:39:05,080
Whatever's on your mind, take it one step at a time.

434
00:39:05,840 --> 00:39:07,240
There's no obstacle

435
00:39:07,360 --> 00:39:08,880
that you can't overcome.

436
00:39:09,120 --> 00:39:10,800
As long as you're still breathing,

437
00:39:10,960 --> 00:39:13,040
anything is possible.

438
00:39:16,920 --> 00:39:17,840
Sir...

439
00:39:18,800 --> 00:39:20,680
Look, if I were planning to end it all,

440
00:39:21,040 --> 00:39:22,320
I wouldn't choose this place.

441
00:39:22,680 --> 00:39:24,600
I'm only here...

442
00:39:28,280 --> 00:39:30,000
for a different place to sleep.

443
00:39:31,120 --> 00:39:32,080
I suppose so.

444
00:39:33,000 --> 00:39:34,240
This place

445
00:39:34,320 --> 00:39:37,040
is meant for the living to lay their sorrows to rest

446
00:39:37,120 --> 00:39:39,520
and move forward with a light heart,

447
00:39:39,960 --> 00:39:42,600
not to find new reasons to grieve.

448
00:39:47,320 --> 00:39:48,440
You're right.

449
00:39:50,400 --> 00:39:52,520
Now it's time for me to...

450
00:39:54,080 --> 00:39:55,200
keep moving forward.

451
00:39:57,440 --> 00:39:58,440
It's getting late.

452
00:39:58,440 --> 00:40:00,880
You should go home. Here, keep this.

453
00:40:11,520 --> 00:40:12,920
Why are you so kind?

454
00:40:14,480 --> 00:40:15,520
God.

455
00:40:30,920 --> 00:40:32,680
Thanks for keeping me company.

456
00:40:35,080 --> 00:40:36,840
I think I'm okay now.

457
00:40:38,360 --> 00:40:39,400
And I've given up

458
00:40:39,440 --> 00:40:41,200
on love and all that

459
00:40:42,080 --> 00:40:43,920
because I've got you, Mom.

460
00:40:44,400 --> 00:40:45,520
Honestly,

461
00:40:45,640 --> 00:40:48,000
I don't have much luck with love, do I?

462
00:40:49,200 --> 00:40:50,200
If I'm not being played,

463
00:40:50,240 --> 00:40:52,320
I'm just being a burden.

464
00:40:53,320 --> 00:40:54,400
I promise

465
00:40:55,920 --> 00:40:57,920
I won't let myself be weak again.

466
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:01,280
Don't you worry, Mom.

467
00:41:01,680 --> 00:41:03,720
Your son...

468
00:41:04,080 --> 00:41:06,520
will take back everything that belongs to him.

469
00:41:19,120 --> 00:41:20,000
I'm off.

470
00:41:24,360 --> 00:41:24,960
Right,

471
00:41:25,600 --> 00:41:27,080
if I fall asleep here again,

472
00:41:27,080 --> 00:41:30,600
please come into my dreams and wake me up.

473
00:41:31,560 --> 00:41:33,000
It's embarrassing.

474
00:41:33,360 --> 00:41:34,800
Good thing that man was kind.

475
00:41:52,080 --> 00:41:52,960
P'Piang,

476
00:41:54,440 --> 00:41:55,600
are you still awake?

477
00:41:56,320 --> 00:41:58,560
Yes, sir. Go ahead.

478
00:41:58,560 --> 00:42:00,360
Did I wake you up?

479
00:42:02,440 --> 00:42:03,600
I think...

480
00:42:07,200 --> 00:42:08,680
I've had enough rest.

481
00:42:09,160 --> 00:42:10,600
Are you free tomorrow?

482
00:42:11,200 --> 00:42:12,360
I need you to come with me.

483
00:42:13,640 --> 00:42:15,320
So you've made up your mind?

484
00:42:15,960 --> 00:42:17,640
I'm starting a new company.

485
00:42:17,680 --> 00:42:20,400
That sounds more like the Mr. Ing I know.

486
00:42:20,440 --> 00:42:21,960
I'm always ready.

487
00:42:22,080 --> 00:42:23,320
See you then.

488
00:42:56,000 --> 00:42:57,440
[From Business Empire to New Beginning,]

489
00:42:57,480 --> 00:42:59,560
[Can He Rise to Glory Again?]

490
00:42:59,560 --> 00:43:01,400
[From Araya Group to NEW ORDER,]

491
00:43:01,440 --> 00:43:04,120
[Can Ing Climb to the Top Again?]

492
00:43:05,120 --> 00:43:06,360
There's a lot of public interest

493
00:43:06,400 --> 00:43:08,840
in your decision to leave Araya Group.

494
00:43:09,040 --> 00:43:10,840
Is there an untold story behind it?

495
00:43:10,920 --> 00:43:11,600
Excuse me.

496
00:43:11,600 --> 00:43:13,880
That question wasn't on the list that we agreed on.

497
00:43:13,880 --> 00:43:15,560
But we're all very curious.

498
00:43:15,600 --> 00:43:17,320
What about your past successes?

499
00:43:17,360 --> 00:43:19,800
Have you truly been able to leave them behind?

500
00:43:19,880 --> 00:43:21,440
Have you actually moved on?

501
00:43:23,720 --> 00:43:25,040
The name "NEW ORDER"

502
00:43:25,040 --> 00:43:26,440
is my answer to that question.

503
00:43:27,720 --> 00:43:28,920
And from now on,

504
00:43:29,080 --> 00:43:30,680
I will never look back again.

505
00:43:31,440 --> 00:43:32,960
I will only keep moving forward.

506
00:43:38,920 --> 00:43:41,680
I've transferred the share we agreed on.

507
00:43:41,880 --> 00:43:43,560
It's time you face reality.

508
00:43:47,240 --> 00:43:49,600
[I've transferred the share we agreed on.]

509
00:43:49,600 --> 00:43:51,840
[It's time you face reality.]

510
00:43:58,600 --> 00:44:00,320
What about your past successes?

511
00:44:00,360 --> 00:44:02,920
Have you truly been able to leave them behind?

512
00:44:03,120 --> 00:44:04,360
The name "NEW ORDER"

513
00:44:04,400 --> 00:44:06,000
is my answer to that question.

514
00:44:21,400 --> 00:44:24,560
I'll return this money to P'Ing on your behalf.

515
00:44:58,080 --> 00:44:59,960
Mom, let me help you.

516
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:02,600
Oh, it's fine. I can do it myself.

517
00:45:02,600 --> 00:45:05,280
See? I'm still strong.

518
00:45:25,040 --> 00:45:28,600
Look at you. Your hair's a total mess.

519
00:45:28,640 --> 00:45:31,400
Did you come straight to see me as soon as you woke up?

520
00:45:31,760 --> 00:45:32,640
Of course.

521
00:45:32,640 --> 00:45:34,920
Why? Do I not look good with messy hair?

522
00:45:38,120 --> 00:45:39,600
Keep thinking you look good, then.

523
00:45:44,480 --> 00:45:45,840
How are you feeling, Mom?

524
00:45:46,400 --> 00:45:48,080
I'm doing fine.

525
00:45:48,080 --> 00:45:49,200
See for yourself.

526
00:46:02,440 --> 00:46:04,800
-I'm doing okay, too. -Really?

527
00:46:04,840 --> 00:46:06,320
Have you eaten yet?

528
00:46:06,720 --> 00:46:07,800
I already have.

529
00:46:13,560 --> 00:46:14,560
Itt, wait.

530
00:46:21,920 --> 00:46:23,040
Your mom...

531
00:46:23,800 --> 00:46:25,080
really loves you.

532
00:46:26,080 --> 00:46:27,280
How did you find this place?

533
00:46:28,720 --> 00:46:29,680
I paid for it.

534
00:46:30,680 --> 00:46:32,800
Consider it deducted from the salary I haven't paid you.

535
00:46:35,120 --> 00:46:36,280
As for the expenses,

536
00:46:37,360 --> 00:46:38,880
I'll pay you back in two days.

537
00:46:40,840 --> 00:46:42,320
I want to handle this myself.

538
00:46:43,320 --> 00:46:44,800
Don't bother coming here again.

539
00:46:47,160 --> 00:46:48,200
My mom has cancer.

540
00:46:48,880 --> 00:46:50,000
I don't want her to get stressed.

541
00:46:53,760 --> 00:46:55,200
You think I wanted to be here?

542
00:46:57,600 --> 00:46:58,360
Here.

543
00:46:59,280 --> 00:47:00,960
Just stay here and take care of your mom.

544
00:47:02,400 --> 00:47:03,160
I'm off.

545
00:47:03,360 --> 00:47:04,240
Don't bother seeing me out.

546
00:47:07,080 --> 00:47:07,960
Hey, wait.

547
00:47:10,840 --> 00:47:11,920
Did you drive here?

548
00:47:16,080 --> 00:47:18,200
Come on, I'm going with you.

549
00:47:34,800 --> 00:47:35,840
No need to lock it.

550
00:47:36,240 --> 00:47:37,400
I'm not going anywhere.

551
00:47:38,000 --> 00:47:39,200
I wasn't planning on it.

552
00:47:41,000 --> 00:47:42,800
Why did you decide to come back?

553
00:47:45,120 --> 00:47:46,280
I'm just hungry.

554
00:48:09,280 --> 00:48:10,080
Itt,

555
00:48:11,760 --> 00:48:13,280
didn't you say you liked me, little brother?

556
00:48:14,040 --> 00:48:15,000
You used to be...

557
00:48:16,600 --> 00:48:18,200
so clingy, Itt.

558
00:48:20,080 --> 00:48:21,960
Why aren't you flirting with me anymore?

559
00:48:24,840 --> 00:48:26,280
My brother wouldn't say that.

560
00:48:26,520 --> 00:48:27,200
Oh, yeah?

561
00:48:28,120 --> 00:48:29,240
What is he supposed to say?

562
00:48:29,320 --> 00:48:30,520
He'd act all high and mighty

563
00:48:31,360 --> 00:48:32,640
and sound annoyed.

564
00:48:36,120 --> 00:48:37,520
You're a pain in the butt.

565
00:48:55,560 --> 00:48:56,640
What have you been up to lately?

566
00:48:57,960 --> 00:48:58,960
Waiting for an opportunity

567
00:48:59,280 --> 00:49:00,840
to see you again, P'Ing.

568
00:49:03,640 --> 00:49:04,800
That brother of yours...

569
00:49:05,840 --> 00:49:07,440
treated you so terribly.

570
00:49:08,560 --> 00:49:10,200
Why do you love him so much?

571
00:49:11,720 --> 00:49:13,880
Why do you have to follow him around?

572
00:49:19,400 --> 00:49:20,360
I wonder that, too.

573
00:49:22,120 --> 00:49:24,960
About that time I tried to force myself on you,

574
00:49:25,880 --> 00:49:27,120
have you forgiven me yet?

575
00:49:29,640 --> 00:49:31,120
But if there's a next time,

576
00:49:33,200 --> 00:49:34,800
I won't let you off so easily.

577
00:49:39,920 --> 00:49:41,960
If you succeed, then what?

578
00:49:43,120 --> 00:49:44,800
Will you keep me locked up forever?

579
00:49:47,240 --> 00:49:49,400
Will that really make you happy, Itt?

580
00:49:54,520 --> 00:49:55,800
No matter what,

581
00:49:57,600 --> 00:50:00,040
I'll never let you go.

582
00:50:08,520 --> 00:50:11,800
Oh, P'Piang. You're here early.

583
00:50:13,440 --> 00:50:14,600
How do you like this place?

584
00:50:16,640 --> 00:50:18,480
Going from a twenty-story building

585
00:50:19,040 --> 00:50:20,520
to just two floors...

586
00:50:20,680 --> 00:50:21,960
Does that feel like a huge step down?

587
00:50:23,000 --> 00:50:24,520
Honestly...

588
00:50:24,960 --> 00:50:25,920
it's nothing.

589
00:50:26,720 --> 00:50:28,080
I'm afraid of heights anyway.

590
00:50:28,720 --> 00:50:30,760
Besides, there's no elevator here.

591
00:50:31,120 --> 00:50:32,520
Taking the stairs...

592
00:50:33,880 --> 00:50:36,040
will help with my varicose veins.

593
00:50:39,920 --> 00:50:41,960
Your regular cafe doesn't deliver this far,

594
00:50:42,040 --> 00:50:43,400
so I tried a new place.

595
00:50:43,880 --> 00:50:46,280
The beans are actually good. Have a taste.

596
00:50:46,280 --> 00:50:47,080
Thank you.

597
00:50:48,640 --> 00:50:49,200
Come on.

598
00:50:49,400 --> 00:50:50,720
Let's head upstairs.

599
00:50:55,440 --> 00:50:56,680
It smells wonderful.

600
00:50:56,840 --> 00:50:58,800
From now on, let's get drinks from this cafe.

601
00:50:58,880 --> 00:51:00,880
Consider it a good fresh start.

602
00:51:01,320 --> 00:51:02,280
Understood.

603
00:51:02,360 --> 00:51:04,520
I would've done it anyway even if you hadn't said that.

604
00:51:06,480 --> 00:51:07,960
Thank you so much, P'Piang.

605
00:51:09,360 --> 00:51:11,000
I will never forget what you've done for me.

606
00:51:11,880 --> 00:51:13,360
It's not just me.

607
00:51:14,880 --> 00:51:16,080
Everyone is here.

608
00:51:17,960 --> 00:51:18,640
Who?

609
00:51:23,880 --> 00:51:25,880
-Surprise. -Surprise.

610
00:51:31,520 --> 00:51:32,520
Sir,

611
00:51:33,040 --> 00:51:34,520
we've all resigned.

612
00:51:35,080 --> 00:51:37,240
Right now, we're officially unemployed.

613
00:51:37,480 --> 00:51:38,360
We're hoping you'll consider

614
00:51:38,400 --> 00:51:40,000
bringing us onto your team.

615
00:51:43,280 --> 00:51:44,720
Should I hire you?

616
00:51:44,760 --> 00:51:47,360
This company doesn't exactly have deep pockets.

617
00:51:48,600 --> 00:51:51,280
That "surprise" was pretty weak, though.

618
00:51:52,120 --> 00:51:54,680
Anyway, shall we get down to business?

619
00:51:54,760 --> 00:51:57,000
Everyone here knows each other.

620
00:51:57,040 --> 00:51:57,800
No outsiders at all.

621
00:51:57,840 --> 00:51:59,240
Let me get straight to the point.

622
00:51:59,720 --> 00:52:02,120
This place might just be a two-story building

623
00:52:02,120 --> 00:52:03,200
with no elevator,

624
00:52:04,120 --> 00:52:05,680
and the capital isn't that much.

625
00:52:06,360 --> 00:52:07,440
But nobody came here

626
00:52:07,480 --> 00:52:09,160
expecting the luxury we had

627
00:52:09,200 --> 00:52:10,480
at Araya Group.

628
00:52:10,480 --> 00:52:11,800
We are here...

629
00:52:13,360 --> 00:52:14,720
to get the work done.

630
00:52:15,080 --> 00:52:16,200
NEW ORDER

631
00:52:16,200 --> 00:52:17,360
means exactly what it says.

632
00:52:18,160 --> 00:52:20,000
From now on, we set the rules

633
00:52:20,040 --> 00:52:21,160
of this industry.

634
00:52:22,280 --> 00:52:23,480
Our first project...

635
00:52:24,120 --> 00:52:24,880
is this.

636
00:52:25,040 --> 00:52:26,440
A shopping mall development project

637
00:52:26,480 --> 00:52:28,160
in partnership with a South Korean giant

638
00:52:28,200 --> 00:52:29,680
opening its first branch in Thailand.

639
00:52:29,720 --> 00:52:30,720
That's the LK Group.

640
00:52:30,760 --> 00:52:32,400
Sure, we've already talked things through,

641
00:52:32,480 --> 00:52:33,680
but ultimately,

642
00:52:34,280 --> 00:52:36,800
we must go through the legal bidding process.

643
00:52:37,040 --> 00:52:39,760
And our biggest competitor is...

644
00:52:41,640 --> 00:52:42,920
Araya Group.

645
00:52:47,880 --> 00:52:48,720
Anyone scared?

646
00:53:21,320 --> 00:53:22,680
It's been a while.

647
00:53:23,800 --> 00:53:25,040
How is the data looking?

648
00:53:25,600 --> 00:53:27,000
Everything has been prepared.

649
00:53:34,480 --> 00:53:36,240
As you all know, Thailand,

650
00:53:36,280 --> 00:53:37,160
especially Bangkok,

651
00:53:37,480 --> 00:53:39,440
is home to countless shopping malls.

652
00:53:39,880 --> 00:53:41,880
For LK Group to break into the Thai market,

653
00:53:42,160 --> 00:53:44,320
the key is creating a clear distinction.

654
00:53:45,240 --> 00:53:46,360
It seems like

655
00:53:46,360 --> 00:53:48,880
he's studied the old projects of Araya Group

656
00:53:48,880 --> 00:53:50,480
inside and out.

657
00:53:51,120 --> 00:53:52,480
He did summarize it well, though.

658
00:53:52,600 --> 00:53:54,600
Unfortunately, it's all outdated data

659
00:53:54,640 --> 00:53:56,760
that we developed and decided not to use.

660
00:53:57,080 --> 00:53:58,760
He just dug it up and memorized it,

661
00:53:58,800 --> 00:54:00,800
polishing the delivery to sound credible.

662
00:54:01,480 --> 00:54:02,480
You're right.

663
00:54:03,520 --> 00:54:05,480
Please place your trust and confidence

664
00:54:06,080 --> 00:54:07,600
in Araya Group.

665
00:54:22,120 --> 00:54:23,600
What Mr. Tottiwa just said

666
00:54:23,640 --> 00:54:25,520
sounds very comprehensive.

667
00:54:26,240 --> 00:54:27,560
However, I have one question.

668
00:54:28,200 --> 00:54:29,560
Can the points you've raised

669
00:54:29,560 --> 00:54:31,520
actually be implemented?

670
00:54:34,320 --> 00:54:36,040
Are you certain that luxury brands

671
00:54:36,040 --> 00:54:36,840
will set up shop in your mall?

672
00:54:36,880 --> 00:54:38,160
Mr. Tiwakorn,

673
00:54:38,640 --> 00:54:40,640
we're supposed to present our own proposal.

674
00:54:40,800 --> 00:54:41,760
This isn't a debate.

675
00:54:41,800 --> 00:54:42,600
My apologies.

676
00:54:42,600 --> 00:54:43,560
To be honest, I don't think

677
00:54:43,560 --> 00:54:45,560
this qualifies as a debate

678
00:54:45,680 --> 00:54:47,280
because I know you can't answer

679
00:54:47,280 --> 00:54:48,920
the question I just asked.

680
00:54:56,320 --> 00:54:59,120
It is true, as Mr. Tottiwa mentioned,

681
00:54:59,160 --> 00:55:00,760
that LK Group needs a strong image,

682
00:55:00,800 --> 00:55:03,120
but that image must be practical.

683
00:55:03,400 --> 00:55:05,240
What LK Group truly needs is

684
00:55:05,280 --> 00:55:06,440
a balance of energy.

685
00:55:06,760 --> 00:55:07,960
The balance I'm referring to

686
00:55:08,000 --> 00:55:09,040
involves the five elements:

687
00:55:09,040 --> 00:55:10,960
earth, metal,

688
00:55:11,360 --> 00:55:13,200
wood, water, and fire.

689
00:55:13,200 --> 00:55:14,240
Certainly,

690
00:55:14,280 --> 00:55:17,040
LK Group's designated site is in a prime location.

691
00:55:17,080 --> 00:55:19,320
As for metal, it represents luxury.

692
00:55:33,600 --> 00:55:35,680
P'Ing, congratulations.

693
00:55:58,920 --> 00:56:01,200
What's up, Mr. Freaking Leo?

694
00:56:03,920 --> 00:56:04,880
What do you want?

695
00:56:04,880 --> 00:56:06,120
Why are you calling me out of the blue?

696
00:56:06,400 --> 00:56:09,960
Well, I wanted to congratulate Mr. Ing

697
00:56:10,160 --> 00:56:12,720
on landing such a massive project.

698
00:56:12,760 --> 00:56:15,320
You always find out so fast, don't you?

699
00:56:16,000 --> 00:56:18,840
Spit it out. What's on your mind?

700
00:56:20,120 --> 00:56:21,720
About what I said last time

701
00:56:21,760 --> 00:56:24,360
that I'd love to work with you...

702
00:56:25,640 --> 00:56:27,880
Oh, sorry about that.

703
00:56:27,880 --> 00:56:29,480
I've recently

704
00:56:29,520 --> 00:56:31,480
taken on a huge project,

705
00:56:31,520 --> 00:56:33,160
so I don't think I have any capital left.

706
00:56:33,520 --> 00:56:35,040
We can work something out regarding the money.

707
00:56:35,120 --> 00:56:38,280
But I'm no expert when it comes to real estate.

708
00:56:38,560 --> 00:56:40,840
Can you be my consultant?

709
00:56:41,080 --> 00:56:44,120
How about you put in thirty percent? I'll cover seventy.

710
00:56:44,120 --> 00:56:45,880
You don't have to pay your share yet.

711
00:56:45,920 --> 00:56:46,600
Sound good?

712
00:56:46,640 --> 00:56:47,680
Wait a minute.

713
00:56:48,440 --> 00:56:51,080
Since when has Mr. Freaking Leo

714
00:56:51,120 --> 00:56:52,640
become so generous?

715
00:56:53,120 --> 00:56:55,320
Tell me the truth. What's the catch?

716
00:56:55,920 --> 00:56:58,320
Can't hide anything from you, can I?

717
00:56:59,080 --> 00:57:02,120
I've got a new partner I can really trust.

718
00:57:02,720 --> 00:57:03,480
Who is it?

719
00:57:03,800 --> 00:57:04,680
Do I know them?

720
00:57:05,400 --> 00:57:07,960
Yeah, I'll introduce you to him.

721
00:57:08,000 --> 00:57:10,120
I'll drop by your party tonight.

722
00:57:10,440 --> 00:57:12,280
Alright, see you there.

723
00:57:12,360 --> 00:57:13,640
Okay, see you.

724
00:57:13,640 --> 00:57:13,680
Okay, see you.

725
00:57:13,680 --> 00:57:13,720
Okay, see you.

726
00:57:21,120 --> 00:57:23,200
Money's just pouring in all of a sudden.

727
00:57:24,600 --> 00:57:25,640
Let's celebrate

728
00:57:25,640 --> 00:57:26,960
landing our first project.

729
00:57:27,480 --> 00:57:29,600
-Cheers. -Yay.

730
00:57:29,840 --> 00:57:32,600
We really did choose the right boss.

731
00:57:33,480 --> 00:57:34,400
Enough.

732
00:57:34,640 --> 00:57:35,640
Don't get all sentimental.

733
00:57:35,680 --> 00:57:37,000
Now, eat up.

734
00:57:37,080 --> 00:57:38,200
Order whatever you want.

735
00:57:38,240 --> 00:57:39,720
-Will do. -Yes, sir.

736
00:57:39,760 --> 00:57:40,760
-Alright. -Come on.

737
00:57:41,440 --> 00:57:42,880
-Congrats, man. -Hey, take this.

738
00:57:43,040 --> 00:57:44,040
-Thanks a lot. -Cheers.

739
00:57:44,080 --> 00:57:44,960
-Bottoms up? -Bottoms up...

740
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:46,760
-Can you? -Definitely. Come on.

741
00:57:48,920 --> 00:57:50,720
-Take it easy. You won't make it home. -Be right back.

742
00:57:50,720 --> 00:57:52,320
-Good. -What about you?

743
00:57:52,360 --> 00:57:54,720
-You bet. -Refill this.

744
00:57:54,760 --> 00:57:56,760
-Refill? -Take it already.

745
00:57:56,920 --> 00:57:57,920
I've been waiting.

746
00:58:00,400 --> 00:58:02,120
No one's going home sober tonight.

747
00:58:07,520 --> 00:58:10,080
Look at you, all happy,

748
00:58:10,120 --> 00:58:11,640
Master Ing.

749
00:58:14,920 --> 00:58:16,040
Just thinking about things.

750
00:58:17,080 --> 00:58:20,240
I'm going to introduce my partner to you tonight.

751
00:58:27,760 --> 00:58:29,200
Here he is.

752
00:58:31,720 --> 00:58:33,680
This kid is something else.

753
00:58:33,720 --> 00:58:34,880
He hasn't even graduated,

754
00:58:34,880 --> 00:58:37,120
but he just put down sixty million in one go.

755
00:58:37,120 --> 00:58:39,960
This new generation is actually terrifying.

756
00:58:51,440 --> 00:58:53,680
I'm going to introduce my partner to you tonight.

757
00:58:53,720 --> 00:58:55,520
You know things aren't good between him and me.

758
00:58:55,600 --> 00:58:57,200
Why would you bring him into this project?

759
00:58:57,200 --> 00:58:58,720
We're business partners now.

760
00:58:58,760 --> 00:58:59,520
Get out of the partnership.

761
00:58:59,560 --> 00:59:00,440
Leave me alone.

762
00:59:00,440 --> 00:59:02,400
Even if the whole world depends on you,

763
00:59:02,400 --> 00:59:04,200
I'll be someone you can depend on.

764
00:59:04,240 --> 00:59:05,240
What did you say?

765
00:59:05,280 --> 00:59:07,640
What's wrong with letting Yok stay for a day or two?

766
00:59:08,800 --> 00:59:09,720
Hello?

767
00:59:12,160 --> 00:59:13,240
Yok.

768
00:59:14,040 --> 00:59:15,080
You lied to me.

769
00:59:16,560 --> 00:59:19,360
I've been missing you so badly. It's killing me.

770
00:59:22,840 --> 00:59:26,120
[The UNCUT version of Fool in Love]

771
00:59:26,120 --> 00:59:29,280
[is exclusively available on iQIYI and iQ.com]
